# Workspace context
This repo, Multi-Vendor-Paws, is the Next.js vendor web portal. It is the home repo for the source of truth (docs/SOURCE_OF_TRUTH.md), shared contracts (docs/contracts) and the web and app parity table (docs/parity.md). The other repos are siblings in the same parent folder.
## Repos
- WEB (home): ./ Multi-Vendor-Paws. Next.js vendor portal. Editable.
- BUYER: ../tinder_paws. Flutter buyer mobile app. Read only unless the task says to edit it.
- PANEL: ../tinderpaws_panel. Flutter web admin panel plus Cloud Functions in functions/. Read only unless the task says to edit it.
- VENDOR APP: ../tender_paws_partner. Flutter vendor mobile app that mirrors the buyer app structure. Does not exist until ticket T0.6. Editable once created.
All repos use the same Firebase project, pets-acd3f, which is production.
## Rules
1. Every task names its working repo and the repos it may edit. Anything not named is read only.
2. Before any git command or edit in a repo, print its path and current branch. Run git with git -C <path>.
3. Never commit to main or master in any repo. Work on dev, or on feature/<name> branches created from dev.
4. Never switch branches or stash in a repo with uncommitted changes. Stop and ask.
5. Do not push unless the task says so.
6. Never run firebase deploy, never deploy rules, indexes or functions, and never run a script that writes to Firebase, unless the task says so.
7. Before editing a repo, read its .cursor/skills and AGENTS.md. Never resolve OPEN or CONFIRM lines. Ask me.
8. A change that touches both WEB and VENDOR APP follows the contract first rule: write docs/contracts/<name>.md in WEB, implement WEB, then APP to the same contract, then update docs/parity.md.
9. No em dashes.
